description:
Implement the Verilog module based on the following description.
You are given a 36-bit input vector in[35:0]. We want to know some relationships between each bit and its neighbour: 
// (1) out_both: Each bit of this output vector should indicate whether both the corresponding input bit and its neighbour to the left are '1'. For example, out_both[34] should indicate if in[34] and in[35] are both 1. Since in[35] has no neighbour to the left, the answer is obvious so we don't need to know out_both[35]. 
// (2) out_any: Each bit of this output vector should indicate whether any of the corresponding input bit and its neighbour to the right are '1'. For example, out_any[2] should indicate if either in[2] or in[1] are 1. Since in[0] has no neighbour to the right, the answer is obvious so we don't need to know out_any[0]. 
// (3) out_different: Each bit of this output vector should indicate whether the corresponding input bit is different from its neighbour to the left. For example, out_different[34] should indicate if in[34] is different from in[35]. For this part, treat the vector as wrapping around, so in[35]'s neighbour to the left is in[0].

module top_module (
	input [35:0] in,
	output [34:0] out_both,
	output [35:1] out_any,
	output [35:0] out_different);

