description:
Design a clock generation circuit that produces two output clock signals (c0 and c1) from a single input clock (inclk0). The circuit uses a 2-bit counter to toggle the output signals: c0 toggles at every full cycle of inclk0, while c1 toggles every second cycle. This allows for the generation of a clock signal at half the frequency of the input clock (c0) and another clock signal at a quarter of the input frequency (c1), thus facilitating multiple clock domains in a digital design.
module top_module(
    inclk0,
    c0,
    c1
);

code:
module top_module(
    inclk0,
    c0,
    c1
);input   inclk0;
output  reg c0;  // Changed from wire to reg
output  reg c1;  // Changed from wire to reg

reg     [1:0] counter;

always @(posedge inclk0) begin
    counter <= counter + 1;
    if (counter == 2'b00) begin
        c0 <= ~c0;
    end
    if (counter == 2'b01) begin
        c1 <= ~c1;
    end
end

endmodule

