description:
Design a 4-bit signed adder that computes the sum of two signed 4-bit inputs, `a` and `b`. The module utilizes a carry generation mechanism to handle the addition of the inputs correctly, considering signed arithmetic. The carry bits are propagated through a combinational logic structure to ensure accurate results even in cases of overflow, making it suitable for applications requiring signed arithmetic operations. The final output is a signed 4-bit sum, which includes the effect of carry management across the bits.
module top_module(
  input signed [3:0] a,
  input signed [3:0] b,
  output signed [3:0] sum
);

code:
module top_module(
  input signed [3:0] a,
  input signed [3:0] b,
  output signed [3:0] sum
);wire [3:0] carry;
  assign carry[0] = 1'b0;

  genvar i;
  generate
    for (i = 1; i < 4; i = i + 1) begin
      assign carry[i] = (a[i-1] & b[i-1]) | (a[i-1] & carry[i-1]) | (b[i-1] & carry[i-1]);
    end
  endgenerate

  assign sum = a + b + {carry[3], carry[3:1]};

endmodule

